[{:db/id 17592186059735 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ce194f41-6fc2-5669-9a9a-5765a4bee419" "question-480f94bc-0561-588e-b570-1657983e06e2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ce194f41-6fc2-5669-9a9a-5765a4bee419" :question/id #uuid "ce194f41-6fc2-5669-9a9a-5765a4bee419" :question/math-academy-id "q-107597" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $(A∧B)∨(A∧¬B).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operations:\n\n- First,  we use the distributive law (conjunction over disjunction):\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨(A∧¬B)≡A∧(B∨¬B)\n$$\n\n- Next,  we use the fact that the disjunction of an expression and its negation is a tautology:\n\n$$\nA∧(B∨¬B)≡A∧\\text{t}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the conjunction of an expression and a tautology gives the initial expression:\n\n$$\nA∧\\text{t}≡A\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨(A∧¬B)≡A.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4691870-3991-5d73-8ef6-aa0282e3a085"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4691870-3991-5d73-8ef6-aa0282e3a085" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4691870-3991-5d73-8ef6-aa0282e3a085" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0f3b6458-283b-571f-9a26-0b7d6458ac1b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0f3b6458-283b-571f-9a26-0b7d6458ac1b" "answer-8c664640-a8d9-540c-a8d0-6eef986b478f" "answer-3fc4643b-2573-5fab-be1c-271a55aba445" "answer-8440357c-e8f4-52a1-a3d2-aa0095777a19" "answer-011a757a-8f28-54ed-ba0e-850164295679"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f3b6458-283b-571f-9a26-0b7d6458ac1b" :answer/id #uuid "0f3b6458-283b-571f-9a26-0b7d6458ac1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c664640-a8d9-540c-a8d0-6eef986b478f" :answer/id #uuid "8c664640-a8d9-540c-a8d0-6eef986b478f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A∨B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fc4643b-2573-5fab-be1c-271a55aba445" :answer/id #uuid "3fc4643b-2573-5fab-be1c-271a55aba445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8440357c-e8f4-52a1-a3d2-aa0095777a19" :answer/id #uuid "8440357c-e8f4-52a1-a3d2-aa0095777a19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-011a757a-8f28-54ed-ba0e-850164295679" :answer/id #uuid "011a757a-8f28-54ed-ba0e-850164295679" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-480f94bc-0561-588e-b570-1657983e06e2" :question/id #uuid "480f94bc-0561-588e-b570-1657983e06e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-216907" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨(¬Y∧Y)].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operations:\n\n- First, we use the fact that the conjunction of a statement and its negation is a contradiction:\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨(¬Y∧Y)]≡¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨\\text{c}]\n$$\n\n- Next, we use the fact that the disjunction of a statement and a contradiction equals the original statement:\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨\\text{c}]≡¬(¬X∨¬Y)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use a De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(¬X∨¬Y)≡¬¬(X∧Y)\n$$\n\n- Finally,  we simplify the double negation:\n\n$$\n¬¬(X∧Y)≡X∧Y\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨(¬Y∧Y)]≡X∧Y\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-40f92c2f-604c-5e5a-be11-f4fdbee5d8ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-40f92c2f-604c-5e5a-be11-f4fdbee5d8ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "40f92c2f-604c-5e5a-be11-f4fdbee5d8ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a345243f-29ba-535f-a9fb-a842f28ed390" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a345243f-29ba-535f-a9fb-a842f28ed390" "answer-d374d92d-3da8-529d-b3c3-8ade1c57d532" "answer-02899baf-379d-5a7f-82